      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write an improved version of the test with better understandability — extracting the regex to a named constant, naming variables clearly, and adding brief comments that explain the intent of each assertion.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version extracts the MD5 crypt output regex into a named constant (`MD5_CRYPT_OUTPUT_PATTERN`) with an explanatory comment, and stores intermediate results in named variables (`hashWithRandom`, `hashWithNullSalt`) so each assertion's intent is immediately clear."
